From: conda-forge onnxruntime-feedstock
Subject: [PATCH] Skip the QMoE expert distribution test when onnx is absent

test_qmoe_expert_distribution.py (new in 1.31.0) and the
tools/python/qmoe_expert_distribution.py module it covers both do a
module-level "import onnx", but tools/ci_build/build.py runs the test
unconditionally, before its explicit "onnx is not installed" gate that
protects the other onnx-dependent tests. onnx is not available when building
onnxruntime on conda-forge, so the run dies with ModuleNotFoundError. Skip the
test with a warning when onnx cannot be imported, mirroring that gate.
---
--- a/tools/ci_build/build.py
+++ b/tools/ci_build/build.py
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 from __future__ import annotations
 
 import contextlib
+import importlib.util
 import json
 import os
 import platform
@@ -1933,7 +1934,9 @@
                 [sys.executable, "onnxruntime_test_python.py"], cwd=cwd, dll_path=dll_path, python_path=python_path
             )
 
-            if not args.disable_contrib_ops:
+            if not args.disable_contrib_ops and importlib.util.find_spec("onnx") is None:
+                log.warning("onnx is not installed. The QMoE expert distribution test will be skipped.")
+            elif not args.disable_contrib_ops:
                 log.info("Testing QMoE expert distribution analysis")
                 run_subprocess(
                     [
